================================================================================
DISCLAIMER & RESEARCH ETHICS
================================================================================

1. Purpose and Scope:
   This project is an independent academic, educational, and interoperability
   research toolkit created to study and improve usability on consumer-owned
   Ola S1 electric vehicles (specifically the Android-based infotainment head unit).

2. Lawful Interoperability & Hardware Ownership:
   All research and development activities were conducted strictly on personally
   owned, fully paid consumer hardware. These activities are carried out under the
   lawful doctrine of interoperability research and hardware freedom, specifically
   Section 52(1)(ab) of the Indian Copyright Act, 1957 (which explicitly permits
   the adaptation and study of computer programs to achieve interoperability with
   other programs), and international Fair Use doctrines.

3. Zero Flash Modification & Vehicle Safety Integrity:
   - This toolkit operates strictly on the non-critical Android Infotainment
     Head Unit (HMI) subsystem.
   - At NO point does this software access, modify, flash, or interfere with
     critical vehicle powertrain controllers, Motor Controller Units (MCU),
     Battery Management Systems (BMS), Electronic Braking Systems (EBS),
     accelerator/throttle controls, or safety sensors.
   - The ADB authorization mechanism operates entirely in volatile system RAM
     via a temporary bind-mount (`mount --bind`). Zero physical partitions or
     read-only flash sectors are modified. A standard vehicle restart immediately
     restores the system to factory pristine state.

4. Intellectual Property & Trademarks:
   All trademarks, service marks, trade names, product names, and logos appearing
   in this repository (including "Ola", "Ola Electric", "MoveOS", and "Android")
   are the property of their respective owners. Their use here is purely nominative
   and descriptive to identify compatible hardware. No affiliation, endorsement,
   or sponsorship by Ola Electric Mobility Ltd. is claimed or implied.

5. Open Source Distribution:
   No proprietary vendor code, copyrighted firmware blobs, or private encryption
   keys are distributed in this repository. All code is independently developed
   open-source software communicating over standard network RPC protocols.

